label ch30_33:
    [   0] m "Hey, do you like horror?"
    [   1] m "I remember we talked about it a little bit when you first joined the club."
    [   2] m "I can enjoy horror novels, but not really horror movies."
    [   3] m "The problem I have with horror movies is that most of them just rely on easy tactics."
    [   4] m "Like dark lighting and scary-looking monsters and jump scares, and things like that."
    [   5] m "It's not fun or inspiring to get scared by stuff that just takes advantage of human instinct."
    [   6] m "But with novels, it's a little different."
    [   7] m "The story and writing need to be descriptive enough to put genuinely disturbing thoughts into the reader's head."
    [   8] m "It really needs to etch them deeply into the story and characters, and just mess with your mind."
    [   9] m "In my opinion, there's nothing more creepy than things just being slightly off."
    [  10] m "Like if you set up a bunch of expectations on what the story is going to be about..."
    [  11] m "...And then, you just start inverting things and pulling the pieces apart."
    [  12] m "So even though the story doesn't feel like it's trying to be scary, the reader feels really deeply unsettled."
    [  13] m "Like they know that something horribly wrong is hiding beneath the cracks, just waiting to surface."
    [  14] m "God, just thinking about it gives me the chills."
    [  15] m "That's the kind of horror I can really appreciate."
    [  16] m "But I guess you're the kind of person who plays cute romance games, right?"
    [  17] m "Ahaha, don't worry."
    [  18] m "I won't make you read any horror stories anytime soon."
    [  19] m "I can't really complain if we just stick with the romance~"
